{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137560",
      "title": "An Alternative Way Of Defining Actions",
      "lectureOrder": 695,
      "videoOrder": 640,
      "sourceHash": "0499274bd2e20b19f00e33b465f07832f25e181464d1312588fd92cae75a329c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 5.7,
          "en": "Instead of defining the action like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.7,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "you could define your own function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.22,
          "end": 11.64,
          "en": "which when called generates an Action object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.64,
          "end": 13.98,
          "en": "Because again, I can't emphasize this enough,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.98,
          "end": 17.67,
          "en": "keep in mind that this thing returned by createAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.67,
          "end": 19.59,
          "en": "which is stored in increment here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.59,
          "end": 21.21,
          "en": "is just a function in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "A function that returns an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.07,
          "en": "with a type and a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.07,
          "end": 28.803,
          "en": "So in the end, that is what you want to rebuild here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.88,
          "end": 33.21,
          "en": "And one very common way of rebuilding a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.21,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "that generates objects in JavaScript is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "of course, to use a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 41.04,
          "en": "So you could export a class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.04,
          "end": 42.993,
          "en": "which maybe is called IncrementAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.58,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "which should actually then implement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 50.07,
          "en": "an interface provided by NgRx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 55.07,
          "en": "the Action interface, which is imported from ngrx/store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.37,
          "end": 60.51,
          "en": "And this interface then simply forces you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.51,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "to implement a type property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 64.863,
          "en": "which should be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "This typically should be a read-only type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.43,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "And that's just an extra TypeScript annotation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 74.03999999999999,
          "en": "which makes it very clear that this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.03999999999999,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "of this property should not be overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.76,
          "end": 79.62,
          "en": "And for one specific action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.62,
          "end": 81.53999999999999,
          "en": "in this case, the IncrementAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "we typically also hard code the type into this action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 87.57300000000001,
          "en": "For example, here, Counter Increment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.58,
          "end": 90.72,
          "en": "Then, to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.72,
          "end": 93.78,
          "en": "that this action can also carry some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.78,
          "end": 97.56,
          "en": "you can simply add a constructor function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.56,
          "end": 100.41,
          "en": "to make it easy to add data to this action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.41,
          "end": 101.583,
          "en": "when it's dispatched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.47999999999999,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "And here, you can then accept the payload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 109.05,
          "en": "let's say, that should be attached to this action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.05,
          "end": 111.18,
          "en": "and to find a type of that payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 112.83,
          "en": "And that could be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.83,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "with a property called name, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 117.87,
          "en": "or it could just be a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.87,
          "end": 120.18,
          "en": "if you know that this action should simply include",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.18,
          "end": 122.28,
          "en": "a number as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.28,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "Or, as I had it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 126.9,
          "en": "we could make sure that the payload is actually an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.9,
          "end": 130.62,
          "en": "that has a value property which then is of type number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.62,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "Though, here, I'll choose a slightly different approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 136.59,
          "en": "and set the payload to a number like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.59,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "And instead of naming it payload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "I'll name it value and add public in front of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 143.28,
          "en": "to use this TypeScript shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "where this will now become a property of the objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "that are created based on this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "so that when we instantiate this IncrementAction class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 156.06,
          "en": "we'll always get an object that has a type property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.06,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "which is of this type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "and that has a value property, which is a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 163.23,
          "en": "And that therefore then gives us an Action object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.23,
          "end": 167.61,
          "en": "that has exactly the same shape as this Action object has,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.61,
          "end": 170.163,
          "en": "once increment is called like a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.21,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "And with that, we have such a class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 176.61,
          "en": "that gives us such an Action object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.61,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "And inside of counter-controls.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 183.18,
          "en": "we could now simply instantiate this class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.18,
          "end": 184.77,
          "en": "like this, IncrementAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.77,
          "end": 187.113,
          "en": "and then pass the value to it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 190.23,
          "en": "And that's, of course, just one way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.23,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "of implementing our own action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "You could use any approach that in the end ensures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 199.29,
          "en": "that you get an Action object that has a type property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.29,
          "end": 201.99,
          "en": "and in this case, also a value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 201.99,
          "end": 203.46,
          "en": "though, as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 204.84,
          "en": "it is totally up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 204.84,
          "end": 206.91,
          "en": "which kind and shape of data you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 206.91,
          "end": 208.383,
          "en": "to attach to your action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 210.93,
          "en": "Here, we can do it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 210.93,
          "end": 213.39,
          "en": "and get rid of this increment import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 213.39,
          "end": 216.27,
          "en": "And now as a last step, I also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 216.27,
          "end": 218.73,
          "en": "that I improve the typing of my reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 218.73,
          "end": 220.53,
          "en": "Of course, this step is optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 220.53,
          "end": 222.57,
          "en": "but I still want to go through it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.57,
          "end": 224.49,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll comment out this import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 224.49,
          "end": 226.98,
          "en": "which at the moment doesn't work anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 226.98,
          "end": 228.84,
          "en": "And in this reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 231.81,
          "en": "I wanna replace any here with a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 231.81,
          "end": 234.3,
          "en": "that actually includes all the actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 234.3,
          "end": 236.133,
          "en": "this reducer should handle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 237,
          "end": 239.82,
          "en": "And for that, we can use a little TypeScript trick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 239.82,
          "end": 242.16,
          "en": "We can export a custom type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 242.16,
          "end": 244.35,
          "en": "by using the type keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 244.35,
          "end": 246.663,
          "en": "and then name our actions here CounterActions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 248.04,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "This name is up to you, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 253.14,
          "en": "And set this equal to all the actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 253.14,
          "end": 256.65,
          "en": "that should be related to this counter part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 256.65,
          "end": 258.09,
          "en": "of this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 258.09,
          "end": 260.73,
          "en": "In this case, that's only the IncrementAction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 260.73,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "But if we had another action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 265.68,
          "en": "we could add it separated by a pipe symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 265.68,
          "end": 267,
          "en": "Like this, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 267,
          "end": 268.62,
          "en": "We don't have this action yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 268.62,
          "end": 271.98,
          "en": "but that's how we could group multiple actions together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 271.98,
          "end": 273.6,
          "en": "into one type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 273.6,
          "end": 275.28,
          "en": "Though, here, I'll get rid of this action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 275.28,
          "end": 276.28,
          "en": "which we don't have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 277.23,
          "end": 279.24,
          "en": "And now we can use CounterActions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 279.24,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "which is a group of all the actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 283.40999999999997,
          "en": "that are related to the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 283.40999999999997,
          "end": 285.84000000000003,
          "en": "as a type instead of any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 285.84000000000003,
          "end": 287.963,
          "en": "Here, we can use CounterActions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 289.26,
          "end": 293.463,
          "en": "Of course, we also must import this from the actions file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 294.42,
          "end": 299.313,
          "en": "And now here, we can indeed use any type that we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 300.54,
          "end": 301.62,
          "en": "And now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 301.62,
          "end": 305.82,
          "en": "you will see that if I try to check for a certain type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 305.82,
          "end": 308.7,
          "en": "TypeScript indeed only suggests me types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 308.7,
          "end": 313.02,
          "en": "that are supported by the CounterActions I defined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 313.02,
          "end": 314.91,
          "en": "and it therefore reduces the danger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 314.91,
          "end": 316.413,
          "en": "of having a typo in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 317.34,
          "end": 321.48,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could even take this one step further,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 321.48,
          "end": 324.6,
          "en": "and we could add another constant here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 324.6,
          "end": 326.82,
          "en": "in our counter.actions file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 326.82,
          "end": 329.07,
          "en": "and maybe name it INCREMENT",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 329.07,
          "end": 332.15999999999997,
          "en": "and store our identifier in this constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 332.15999999999997,
          "end": 334.89,
          "en": "so that we have only one place where we store this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 334.89,
          "end": 336.75,
          "en": "and we then export this constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 336.75,
          "end": 339.79,
          "en": "And we then simply use this constant here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 341.28,
          "end": 346.28,
          "en": "and also here by importing it and using it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 347.79,
          "end": 349.71,
          "en": "And now we have only one place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 349.71,
          "end": 351.45,
          "en": "where we define this identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 351.45,
          "end": 354.39,
          "en": "And then in all the places where we use the identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 354.39,
          "end": 355.95,
          "en": "we just use this constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 355.95,
          "end": 360.27,
          "en": "hence further reducing the danger of having a typo in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 360.27,
          "end": 362.73,
          "en": "And all this is totally optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 362.73,
          "end": 365.61,
          "en": "and of course, it is some extra work, but in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 365.61,
          "end": 367.23,
          "en": "it's what happens under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 367.23,
          "end": 369.24,
          "en": "when you're using createAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 369.24,
          "end": 371.49,
